title: 'state-machine: invalidate storage transaction cache on state version change'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Fix a cache-bleed bug in `OverlayedChanges::storage_transaction_cache`. The cache stored the
    pre-computed storage root and transaction without recording which `StateVersion` was used to
    build them. After calling `storage_root(V0)`, a subsequent `storage_root(V1)` (or
    `child_storage_root` / `drain_storage_changes` with a different version) would return the
    cached V0 result, even though V0 and V1 produce different roots for state containing values
    that exceed `TRIE_VALUE_NODE_THRESHOLD`.

    The cache now stores the `state_version` it was built with and is invalidated and recomputed
    whenever a different version is requested. A regression test exercises the V0 → V1 → V0
    transition with a value larger than the inline threshold.

crates:
- name: sp-state-machine
  bump: patch
